  "body": "Stacked on #2135 (merge #2135 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `Tilt::refusal` in `crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs` and wired it into `OpParams::named_refusal` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs`). Out-of-range tilt angles now refuse by name with the field (`Tool axis A` or `Tool axis B`), the canonical limits (`-90..90` and `-180..180`), and the `A 0` / `B 180` pose for the face opposite the top.\n- Updated `apply_hint` in `crates/ui/src/feedback.rs` to show `draft.named_refusal()` before the generic unusable-value text.\n- Updated `TiltedFrame::new` in `crates/cl/src/cl/frame.rs` to zero out axis components smaller than `1e-12` when selecting the tie-breaking seed axis. The `A 0` / `B 180` frame now keeps plane X along machine `+X` (the A rotary axis).\n- Updated `site/content/guide/getting-started/first-4axis-part.md`, `crates/app/tests/first_4axis_part.rs`, and `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` so `Flat A180` uses the same `-0.75, 0` to `-0.25, 0` ends as the other three flats.\n- Saved `Tilt.basis_version` with each tilted operation. A missing version uses basis 0 and preserves the original coordinates and digest. New UI and MCP drafts use basis 1 with a distinct cache stamp. The loader refuses an unknown basis version.\n- Advanced the project format from version 62 to version 63. Older builds refuse these saved files instead of ignoring `basis_version` and rotating regenerated cuts.\n- Recorded the design choices in `docs/decisions/2133-tilt-a180-refusal-basis.md`.\n\n## Apply hint screenshots\n\nThese images render the shipping shell with egui_kittest. Both images show the same Face draft at A 180 and B 0.\nThe viewport uses the harness placeholder. The operation page and the Apply hint use the shipping widgets.\nThe before image uses `feedback.rs` from parent `06dfbcaafab3e6bc98fd2cbed85c9ee884bbfd2c`.\nThe after image uses `feedback.rs` from reviewed head `e955c9dfed47e7c2d1ce0a73ffd335fa72c04a99`.\nThe capture code and logs remain outside the PR branch. The images exist only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: generic Apply hint](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/6a3b0cc6a54d84170edbc852a85f4bf5ce00f25e/2157/before-apply-hint.png) | ![After: angle limits and A0 B180 remedy](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/6a3b0cc6a54d84170edbc852a85f4bf5ce00f25e/2157/after-apply-hint.png) |\n\nThe test `apply_hint_names_tilt_limits_and_a0_b180_remedy` fails with the parent source (exit 101).\nIt passes after the reviewed source is restored (exit 0).\n\n## Cause\n\n1. `Tilt::is_sane` returned `bool` with no entry in `OpParams::named_refusal`. `CreateOperation`, `EditOperationParams`, MCP `add_operation`/`edit_operation`, and the UI Apply hint fell back to generic \"not usable\" text without stating the limits or the `A 0` / `B 180` pose.\n2. `TiltedFrame::from_angles(origin, 0.0, 180.0)` produces `axis[0] = sin(180 deg) ~ 1.22e-16` while `axis[1] = 0.0`. `TiltedFrame::new` compared magnitudes without a float-dust threshold, picked the Y axis as seed instead of X, and swapped plane X and Y on the `A 0` / `B 180` face.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Pinning tests (red before fix, green after fix):**\n  - `cl::tests::a0_b180_frame_keeps_plane_x_on_machine_x` (`crates/cl/src/cl/tests.rs`): failed before fix (`u=[0.0, 1.0, 0.0]`), passes after fix.\n  - `tilt_a180::out_of_range_tilt_refuses_by_name_with_a0_b180_remedy` (`crates/app/tests/tilt_a180.rs`): failed before fix (`operation parameters are not usable for a Slot operation`), passes after fix for `CreateOperation`, `EditOperationParams`, MCP `add_operation`, and MCP `edit_operation`.\n  - `tilt_a180::a0_b180_slot_cuts_along_machine_x_like_the_other_faces` (`crates/app/tests/tilt_a180.rs`): failed before fix (cut ran along Y at X ~ 0), passes after fix (cuts along X and posts `G0 A180`).\n  - `feedback::apply_hint_names_tilt_limits_and_a0_b180_remedy` (`crates/ui/tests/feedback.rs`): failed before fix (`check a deg, b deg, origin - the value is not usable`), passes after fix.\n  - `first_4axis_part` (3 tests, ok) and `site/tests/test_first_4axis_part.py` (12 tests, ok).\n- **Compatibility pins (`tilt_basis_compat`):**\n  - `old_project_keeps_basis_status_regeneration_and_posted_cut` checks an old project at load, status, regeneration, and posting.\n  - `corrected_basis_rejects_a_legacy_cache_stamp` checks that basis 1 does not accept a basis 0 cache.\n  - `live_json_tilts_use_current_basis_and_preserve_an_explicit_legacy_basis` checks the live JSON version defaults and an explicit basis 0.\n  - `unknown_saved_basis_is_visibly_refused_before_loading` checks the visible refusal for an unknown saved basis.\n- **Mutation checks:**\n  - Reverted `crates/cl/src/cl/frame.rs` to `upstream/main`: `a0_b180_frame_keeps_plane_x_on_machine_x` failed; restored: passed.\n  - Reverted `crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs` to `upstream/main`: `out_of_range_tilt_refuses_by_name_with_a0_b180_remedy` failed; restored: passed.\n  - Reverted `crates/ui/src/feedback.rs` to `upstream/main`: `apply_hint_names_tilt_limits_and_a0_b180_remedy` failed; restored: passed.\n- **Gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, batch fallback):**\n  - Steps `[01]`–`[07]` (`geometry`, `kernel`, `cl`, `tools`, `post`, `sim`, `motion`) passed on this tree; `[08]` was interrupted by a server restart, then `--only clippy` (`clippy -D warnings`, 441s), `--only ui` (`ui suites`, 52s), and `--only app` (`app suites`, 1492s) each ran and passed with 0 failures. `xtask` `gate_maps_tests` passed (8 tests, ok).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- None. Zero `.nc` or `.cl` files changed against `base-2135` (`examples/first-4axis-part.nc` stayed byte-identical). `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` updates `Flat A180`'s `a` and `b`, states `basis_version: 1` for tilted operations, and updates their cache stamps. All cached move coordinates match. The example NC file is unchanged.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `zola build` and the three `site/tests` tests that invoke `zola` (`zola` is not installed on this host).\n- Interactive GUI click-through or physical machine cut.\n- Release-lane heavy binaries (`motion:finish3d`, `motion:pivot5d`, `motion:flow`, `app:center_cut_multiaxis`) and UI pixel snapshots.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- **Stacked on #2135 (`issue/1904-first-4axis-part`):** edits `site/content/guide/getting-started/first-4axis-part.md`, `crates/app/tests/first_4axis_part.rs` (`build`, `each_flat_posts_the_same_cut_after_its_index`), and `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj`. Merge #2135 first.\n- **Same files, different functions/lines (whichever merges second refreshes):**\n  - `crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs`: PRs #2126, #2093, #2037, #1817, #1713 touch `OpParams` variants; this PR touches the `Tilt` structure and its implementation.\n  - `crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs`: PRs #2126, #2093, #2037, #1817 touch other operations or checks; this PR adds a tilt guard at the start of `OpParams::named_refusal`.\n\nChangelog: refuse out-of-range 3+2 tilt angles by name with the A0 B180 hint and keep A0 B180 plane X along machine X\nEffort: high (no escalation)\nFixes #2133\n\n\n",
